{
  "abstract": "The complete k-partite graph K_{2,...,2} is k-choosable (Erdős, Rubin and Taylor 1979). It is a case of Ohba's conjecture (2002) that ch(G) = χ(G) whenever G has at most 2χ(G)+1 vertices, which Noel, Reed and Wu proved in 2015. This package formalizes only the Erdős–Rubin–Taylor case, by a direct induction with Hall's theorem. The analogous question for parts of size three is harder: ch(K_{3*k}) = ⌈(4k−1)/3⌉ (Kierstead 2000).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Wentao Li"
    }
  ],
